            <ArticleTitle>Rhodium-catalyzed carbonylative synthesis of silyl-substituted indenones.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13149-13152</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc08210j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel and efficient rhodium-catalyzed procedure for the preparation of silyl-substituted indenones has been developed. Using silanes and internal alkynes as the substrates, in the presence of CO, good to excellent yields of the desired indenones were isolated. A wide range of functional groups, encompassing esters, amines, nitriles and halides, is compatible in this system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
